-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura over a DVR with Galois-equivariant quotient of Tₚ J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ that is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra, and its fraction field $K$, regarded as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra compatibly with $O$ (scalar tower), subject to the hypothesis that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Give $\mathrm{JZero}\,N = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ its `heckeModuleBar` module structure over `HeckeAlg`, let $T_p =$ [`TateModule p (JZero N)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the group of sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, and let `rationalHeckeAlgebra` be the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes T_p)$ generated by the image of `rationalHeckeRep`. Then for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda$ from that subalgebra to $K$ which sends the image of each $c \in \mathbb{Z}_p \subseteq \mathbb{Q}_p$ to the image of $c$ in $K$, there exists $\rho$ of type [`GaloisRepAdic O`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is a free finite $O$-module $\rho.V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_O(\rho.V)$ satisfying [`GaloisActionIsAdicContinuous`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L9), such that: (1) for every prime $\ell \nmid Np$ and every $a \in O$ with $\Lambda$ of the Hecke generator `heckeGen ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩` equal to the image of $a$ in $K$, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ is $X^2 - aX + \ell$; (2) for every prime $\ell \nmid Np$, every valuation subring with $\ell$ a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in its inertia subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$, $\rho.\rho\,\sigma = 1$; (3) there is a surjective $K$-linear map $\pi : K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p \to K \otimes_O \rho.V$ with $\pi \circ (\text{base change of } \sigma\text{-action on } T_p) = (\text{base change of } \rho.\rho\,\sigma) \circ \pi$ for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction in the form needed for the Frey curve argument: a $p$-adic character of the Hecke algebra acting on the Tate module of $J_0(N)$ gives a two-dimensional $O$-adic Galois representation with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes away from $Np$, together with the extra information that the representation is realised as a Galois-equivariant quotient of $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_0(N)$. It feeds into [`CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_of_point_tateModule_jZero_quotient`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_of_point_tateModule_jZero_quotient), where the character is the one attached to an eigenform.
